{"name":"Cockscomb Red","hex":"#bc5378","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cockscomb","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The fleshy red crest of a rooster.","A red cap once worn by court jesters."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cockscomb"},{"term":"red","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of the setting sun, blood, and strawberries; the color which is evoked by the longest visible wavelengths (between about 625–740 nm), and a primary additive color.","A revolutionary socialist or (most commonly) a Communist;  a Bolshevik, a supporter of the Bolsheviks in the Russian Civil War."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a red hue.","Having an orange-brown or orange-blond colour; ginger."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Comb (anatomy)","blocks":[{"text":"A comb is a fleshy growth or crest on the top of the head of some gallinaceous birds, such as domestic chickens. The alternative name cockscomb reflects the fact that combs are generally larger on cock birds than on hens. The comb is one of several fleshy protuberances on the heads of chickens, the others being the wattles and earlobes, which collectively are called caruncles. In turkeys, the caruncles are the fleshy nodules on the head and throat."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Rooster_portrait2_%28cropped_2%29.jpg/330px-Rooster_portrait2_%28cropped_2%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Comb_(anatomy)"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Zijaanzichtkophaan.JPG/120px-Zijaanzichtkophaan.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Zijaanzichtkophaan.JPG/250px-Zijaanzichtkophaan.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Zijaanzichtkophaan.JPG/120px-Zijaanzichtkophaan.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZijaanzichtkophaan.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/CHUCK_-_Flickr_-_Cornelia_Kopp.jpg/120px-CHUCK_-_Flickr_-_Cornelia_Kopp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/CHUCK_-_Flickr_-_Cornelia_Kopp.jpg/250px-CHUCK_-_Flickr_-_Cornelia_Kopp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/CHUCK_-_Flickr_-_Cornelia_Kopp.jpg/120px-CHUCK_-_Flickr_-_Cornelia_Kopp.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACHUCK_-_Flickr_-_Cornelia_Kopp.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Haushuhn_%D9%85%D8%B1%D8%BA_%D8%AE%D8%A7%D9%86%DA%AF%DB%8C_06.jpg/120px-Haushuhn_%D9%85%D8%B1%D8%BA_%D8%AE%D8%A7%D9%86%DA%AF%DB%8C_06.jpg?utm_source=en.wi